        <item>
            <title>0.27.4</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:28:23 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>64</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.4</h3><ul><li>Monitors can now end on any date, or never. Settings &gt; Monitors has an Ends control (On a date or Never) with quick Extend buttons, and the 30-day limit is gone. AI apps still set 24 hours unless you or they choose otherwise.</li><li>The details sheet of an ended monitor scrolls again.</li><li>A monitor set to never end stays that way: when ChatGPT renews it, Keeploop no longer adds an end date or moves an end date earlier.</li><li>Claude Code sessions that move to another git worktree of the same project no longer duplicate their monitors. When the old worktree folder is gone, its monitor moves to the new one; otherwise the AI app is told about the monitor in the other worktree and can move it. A monitor whose session is still open is never moved.</li><li>The monitor sheet's button now says Close, and rows no longer blur behind the buttons.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
